  "title": "Comprehensive Antimagnetic Rotation Systematics, Double Shears Dynamics, and Diagnostic Ratio Audit",
  "physics_summary": {
    "spatial_time_reversal_symmetry": "In AMR, two identical high-j blades (e.g. pi(g9/2)^-1) are oriented symmetrically at angles +theta and -theta with respect to the rotation axis z. Under spatial rotation R_z(pi), blade 1 transforms into blade 2, preserving the mean field. Under time reversal T, all spins reverse. The combined symmetry R_z(pi) conserves signature r = e^(-i pi alpha) = +1, strictly forbidding Delta I = 1 M1 transitions (B(M1) = 0). Transverse magnetic dipole moments cancel identically: mu_perp = mu_1_perp + mu_2_perp = g_h j_h sin(theta) - g_h j_h sin(theta) = 0.",
    "radiation_power_law": "The quadrupole transition operator in the transverse plane is Q_22 = sqrt(3/8) (Q_xx - Q_yy) = sqrt(27/8) Q_0 sin^2(theta). The reduced transition probability is B(E2; I -> I-2) = (15 / 32pi) (eQ_eff)^2 sin^4(theta). The fourth-power dependence causes an abrupt, plunging drop of B(E2) in pure AMR (dropping by a factor of 10-20 as theta closes from 90 deg to 15 deg in 106,108Cd). In contrast, in 110Cd, half-rigid core rotation (Im = 19.5 hbar^2/MeV) shares 18% to 26% of the angular momentum, moderating the closure to theta = 70 deg -> 31 deg, maintaining a robust B(E2) plateau (0.14 -> 0.06 e^2b^2).",
    "diagnostic_ratio_threshold": "Normal deformed collective rotors (e.g. 166Er) exhibit large B(E2) ~ 1.5 - 2.0 e^2b^2 (hundreds of W.u.) and dynamic moments of inertia J(2) ~ 35 - 45 hbar^2/MeV, yielding J(2)/B(E2) ~ 15 - 30 hbar^2 MeV^-1 (e^2 b^2)^-1. In contrast, all verified AMR bands in Cd and Pd isotopes exhibit J(2)/B(E2) in the range 100 - 1300 hbar^2 MeV^-1 (e^2 b^2)^-1, exceeding normal collective rotation by more than one full order of magnitude. This giant ratio is an exclusive signature of shears-driven generation of rotational energy without substantial core quadrupole deformation."
  },
